{color.GG}startup.conf {color.N}defines startup behavior and runtime settings for {color.GG}Ares Framework{color.N}.

Available keys:
{color.PP}home {color.WW}= {color.YY}~{color.N}
    Path used by {color.GG}rhome.so {color.N}to set $HOME.
    Supports ~, $var, and absolute paths.

{color.PP}toolkit {color.WW}= {color.YY}$__aresroot__/bin, <+readonly>{color.N}
    Paths registered to $PATH by {color.GG}dynap.so{color.N}.
    <+readonly> marks $PATH as readonly.
    <-readonly> disables the readonly flag.

{color.PP}chmod_toolkit {color.WW}= {color.YY}true{color.N}
    Whether the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}changes permissions for toolkit files ($__aresroot__/bin/*) at startup.

{color.PP}remove_log {color.WW}= {color.YY}false{color.N}
    Whether the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}removes logs from ~/.ares_log/* at startup.

{color.PP}remove_binext {color.WW}= {color.YY}true{color.N}
    Whether the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}removes tool extensions in $__aresroot__/bin/* at startup.
    Example: myscript.sh becomes myscript.
    Duplicate names are handled.

{color.PP}remove_gscache {color.WW}= {color.YY}false{color.N}
    Whether the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}removes GoScript cache files from $TMPDIR/ares/goscript_cache/* at startup.

{color.PP}remove_cscache {color.WW}= {color.YY}false{color.N}
    Whether the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}removes CScript cache files from $TMPDIR/ares/cscript_cache at startup.

{color.PP}startup_hint {color.WW}= {color.YY}true{color.N}
    Whether the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}displays startup hints.

{color.PP}cursor {color.WW}= {color.YY}blink-underline{color.N}
    Wheter the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}to sets the terminal cursor style.
    Available styles:
        {color.R}- {color.GG}native{color.N}
        {color.R}- {color.GG}default{color.N}
        {color.R}- {color.GG}block{color.N}
        {color.R}- {color.GG}blink-block{color.N}
        {color.R}- {color.GG}line{color.N}
        {color.R}- {color.GG}blink-line{color.N}
        {color.R}- {color.GG}underline{color.N}
        {color.R}- {color.GG}blink-underline{color.N}

{color.PP}prompt {color.WW}= {color.YY}true{color.N}
    Whether the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}enables the prompt engine.

{color.PP}prompt_engine {color.WW}= {color.YY}yumipr{color.N}
    Wheter the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}to selects the prompt engine.

{color.PP}yumipr_theme {color.WW}= {color.YY}themes/default.lua{color.N}
    Specifies the theme used by {color.GG}yumipr{color.N}.

{color.PP}suggestion {color.WW}= {color.YY}false{color.N}
    Whether the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}enables the real-time autosuggestion engine.
    Enabling it with "suggestion = true" triggers a warning by default.
    Use "suggestion = true --force" to suppress the warning.

{color.PP}suggestion_engine {color.WW}= {color.YY}shgest{color.N}
    Wheter the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}to selects the autosuggestion engine.

{color.PP}cnf {color.WW}= {color.YY}true{color.N}
    Whether the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}enables the Command Not Found handler.

{color.PP}cnf_engine {color.WW}= {color.YY}cnf_handler{color.N}
    Wheter the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}to selects the Command Not Found engine.

{color.PP}lock_variable {color.WW}= {color.YY}true{color.N}
    Whether {color.GG}dynav.so {color.N}and the {color.GG}bootloader {color.N}mark Ares Framework variables as readonly.

Engine paths:
Keys ending in _engine select modules from $__aresroot__/init/engine/.
The key name determines the engine category.

Example:
{color.PP}cnf_engine {color.WW}= {color.YY}yourcustom_cnf{color.N}
{color.PP}suggestion_engine {color.WW}= {color.YY}shgest{color.N}

Loads:
    {color.R}- {color.GG}$__aresroot__/init/engine/cnf/yourcustom_cnf.shx{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}$__aresroot__/init/engine/suggestion/shgest.shx{color.N}